{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/social-barrier",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "social barrier"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "stigma, prejudice, stereotyping, low expectations, and discriminatory practices that marginalise disabled individuals in education, employment, healthcare, and social interactions."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "Unlike physical or environmental obstacles, social barriers are rooted in how society perceives and treats disability, often viewing it as a personal deficit rather than a result of exclusionary structures. Social barriers manifest in various ways: inaccessible communication, lack of representation in decision-making, patronising attitudes, and institutional policies that fail to accommodate diverse needs. Overcoming them requires cultural change, awareness-raising, and the active involvement of disabled people in shaping inclusive practices and policies."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "4.4.4"
  ],
